      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Even a \"tiny bit\" of extra Vitamin K can cause a significant enough shift in your INR to be dangerous when you are on warfarin. Dosing adjustments should never be made by the patient; the medication dosage is calibrated for your specific needs. To safely support your bone health, focus on a balanced, consistent diet rich in calcium and magnesium, and discuss specific, controlled dietary strategies with your physician. Do not attempt to self-dose supplements to manage a serious medication like warfarin.",
      "source": "target",
